{"name":"Drover","hex":"#fbeb9b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"drover","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who drives animals (which are on foot or on the hoof, walking to some destination), especially cattle or sheep, and especially over long distances."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drover"}],"entries":[{"title":"Droving","blocks":[{"text":"Droving is the practice of walking livestock over long distances. It is a type of herding, often associated with cattle, in which case it is a cattle drive. Droving stock to market—usually on foot and often with the aid of dogs—has a very long history. An owner might entrust an agent to deliver stock to market and bring back the proceeds. There has been droving since people in cities found it necessary to source food from distant supplies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Morning_by_ST_Gill.jpg/330px-Morning_by_ST_Gill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Droving"},{"title":"Drover (Australian)","blocks":[{"text":"A drover in Australia is a person, typically an experienced stockman, who moves livestock, usually sheep, cattle, and horses \"on the hoof\" over long distances. Reasons for droving may include: delivering animals to a new owner's property, taking animals to market, or moving animals during a drought in search of better feed and/or water or in search of a yard to work on the livestock. The drovers who covered very long distances to open up new country were known as \"overlanders\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Drovers%2C_Roseneath_sheep_station%2C_Tenterfield%2C_1942_-_unknown_photographer_for_Walkabout_magazine_%285038009366%29.jpg/330px-Drovers%2C_Roseneath_sheep_station%2C_Tenterfield%2C_1942_-_unknown_photographer_for_Walkabout_magazine_%285038009366%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drover_(Australian)"},{"title":"Drover (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Drover was a British company providing vehicle subscriptions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drover_(company)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg/500px-Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg/500px-Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drovers in New Zealand c. 1950","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_(11313111916).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/500px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/1280px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/500px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern small-scale cattle drive in New Mexico, U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACattle_round_up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Edwin_Henry_Landseer_%281802-1873%29_-_The_Drover%27s_Departure%2C_A_Scene_in_the_Grampians_-_FA.88%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg/500px-Edwin_Henry_Landseer_%281802-1873%29_-_The_Drover%27s_Departure%2C_A_Scene_in_the_Grampians_-_FA.88%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c